{
    "background_story": "Julie was a marine biologist with a passion for studying the ocean's apex predators. Her specialty was the mycteroperca, a genus of large groupers found in the warm waters of the Atlantic and Pacific. Julie spent years researching the behavior and habitat of these magnificent creatures, earning her the nickname 'Grouper Guru' among her peers. Her groundbreaking research on the mycteroperca's role in maintaining the balance of coral reef ecosystems was published in several prestigious scientific journals. Julie's dedication to her work took her to the most remote and exotic locations, from the Caribbean to the Great Barrier Reef. Her love for the mycteroperca was contagious, inspiring a new generation of marine biologists to follow in her footsteps and continue her vital work.",
